h":37,"ar_uthmani":"فَتَقَبَّلَهَا رَبُّهَا بِقَبُولٍ حَسَنٍ وَأَنۢبَتَهَا نَبَاتًا حَسَنًا وَكَفَّلَهَا زَكَرِيَّا ۖ كُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا ٱلْمِحْرَابَ وَجَدَ عِندَهَا رِزْقًا ۖ قَالَ يَـٰمَرْيَمُ أَنَّىٰ لَكِ هَـٰذَا ۖ قَالَتْ هُوَ مِنْ عِندِ ٱللَّهِ ۖ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَرْزُقُ مَن يَشَآءُ بِغَيْرِ حِسَابٍ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Her Lord graciously accepted her and made her grow in goodness, and entrusted her to the charge of Zachariah. Whenever Zachariah went in to see her in her sanctuary, he found her supplied with provisions. He said, ‘Mary, how is it you have these provisions?’ and she said, ‘They are from God: God provides limitlessly for whoever He will.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"فَتَقَبَّلَهَا","en_gloss":"So accepted her","transliteration":"fataqabbalahā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":2,"ar":"رَبُّهَا","en_gloss":"her Lord","transliteration":"rabbuhā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":3,"ar":"بِقَبُولٍ","en_gloss":"with acceptance","transliteration":"biqabūlin","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":4,"ar":"حَسَنٍۢ","en_gloss":"good","transliteration":"ḥasanin","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَأَنۢبَتَهَا","en_gloss":"and reared her ","transliteration":"wa-anbatahā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":6,"ar":"نَبَاتًا","en_gloss":"a rearing","transliteration":"nabātan","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":7,"ar":"حَسَنًۭا","en_gloss":"good","transliteration":"ḥasanan","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":8,"ar":"وَكَفَّلَهَا","en_gloss":"and put her in (the) care","transliteration":"wakaffalahā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":9,"ar":"زَكَرِيَّا ۖ","en_gloss":"(of) Zakariya","transliteration":"zakariyyā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":10,"ar":"كُلَّمَا","en_gloss":"Whenever","transliteration":"kullamā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":11,"ar":"دَخَلَ","en_gloss":"entered","transliteration":"dakhala","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":12,"ar":"عَلَيْهَا","en_gloss":"upon her","transliteration":"ʿalayhā","verse_key":"3:37"},{"pos":13,"ar":"زَكَرِيَّا","en_gloss":"Zakariya","transliteration":"zakariyyā","ve